course: dictionary
lesson: 4123
title: A word from the glassworks
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A glassblower is a person who makes glass things, like vases and bottles. Look at the word's parts: glass and blower. A glassblower blows, so the word hints at the job: they blow into glass. That is a clue, and you can check it in the sentence.
explain: «Hot glass is soft like toffee: a glassblower blows into a blob of it on a long pipe and it swells into a bubble that becomes a vase.» The clues are soft like toffee, blob, pipe and bubble. They show what the glassblower does, so a glassblower shapes hot glass by blowing into it.
explain: «Glassblowers shape glass that is over 1000 °C, when it is soft and stretchy.» Over 1000 °C is very hot. Hot glass is soft, so it can be shaped. Glassblowing is the word for the craft itself.
fact: A glassblower makes glass objects, like vases and bottles, by blowing air through a long tube into hot, melted glass.
fact: Glass gets soft and runny when it is very hot, and hard again when it cools.
fact: Glassblowing is an old craft, used since Roman times.
fact: Glassblowers work near a furnace that is over 1,000 °C, and they wear protection to stay safe.
fact: «Glassblowers» is the plural: more than one person who does this work. «Glassblowing» is the craft itself.
exercise: «Hot glass is soft like toffee: a glassblower blows into a blob of it on a long pipe.» What does a glassblower do? | Cuts cold glass with a saw | *Blows air into hot, melted glass to shape it | Bakes toffee in a kitchen | Paints pictures on windows
exercise: Ella says a glassblower must be someone who cuts glass, because of the word glass. Is she right? | Yes, a glassblower works only with cold glass | No, a glassblower only sells glass in shops | *No, a glassblower blows into hot glass to shape it | Yes, cutting is the only job with glass
exercise: «Glassblowers shape glass that is over 1000 °C.» What does over 1000 °C mean? | *Hotter than 1,000 degrees | Less than 100 degrees | Exactly 1,000 degrees, every time | Colder than 1,000 degrees
test: «Glassblowers shape glass that is over 1000 °C, when it is soft and stretchy.» What does soft and stretchy suggest? | It is painted green | *It can be shaped while it is hot | It cannot be touched by anyone | It is cold and very hard
test: What is glassblowing? | A way of cleaning old windows | A type of cooking with sugar | *The craft of making glass objects by blowing into hot glass | A kind of sport played on ice
exam: Which sentence best explains what a glassblower is? | *A glassblower is a person who blows hot, melted glass through a tube to make vases and bottles | A glassblower is a person who paints on glass with a brush | A glassblower is a person who sells glass in a shop | A glassblower is a person who cuts glass into windows
